From: rtw89-usb-ap-fix <local@patch>
Date: 2026-05-05
Subject: [PATCH 0004] rtw89: mac80211: skip MAC-level flush in ops_flush for USB AP

The existing patch 0003 skips rtw89_mac_flush_txq() in the set_key
DISABLE_KEY path for USB AP mode. However the identical timeout also
fires from the ops_flush mac80211 callback, which mac80211 calls to
drain a station's TX queue before removing it on every disconnect.

With a USB HCI, the MAC DLE (Data Link Engine) cannot drain within the
default 50 ms poll window.  The resulting "timed out to flush queues"
leaves the DLE in an inconsistent state.  Over many connect/disconnect
cycles (typically 1-3 days of continuous AP operation) the accumulated
state corruption causes the AP to stop sending 802.11 beacons, making
the SSID invisible to clients until the device is hard-rebooted.

The HCI-level rtw89_hci_flush_queues() called just before is sufficient
to prevent TX stalls.  Skip rtw89_mac_flush_txq() in ops_flush when the
device is a USB adapter operating in AP mode, consistent with patch 0003.

Additionally rename the single-use helper added in patch 0003 to the
more generic rtw89_is_usb_ap() so it can be shared by both call sites
without confusion.

Symptoms fixed:
  kern.info: rtw89_8922au_git 2-1:1.0: timed out to flush queues
  (fired on every client disconnect; AP becomes invisible after 1-3 days)

Tested-on: RTL8922AU (0bda:8912) USB3, iStoreOS aarch64, kernel 6.6.119
Applies-after: 0003-rtw89-mac80211-skip-usb-ap-key-disable-flush.patch
---
 mac80211.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index e96126d..2d4a7f3 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -954,14 +954,16 @@ static int rtw89_ops_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	return __rtw89_ops_sta_state(hw, vif, sta, old_state, new_state);
 }
 
-static bool rtw89_ops_skip_usb_ap_key_disable_flush(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
-					       struct ieee80211_vif *vif)
+/*
+ * rtw89_is_usb_ap - true when running as USB adapter in AP mode.
+ * Shared guard for all MAC-level flush paths that reliably time out on
+ * USB because the DLE cannot drain within the 50 ms default window.
+ */
+static bool rtw89_is_usb_ap(struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev,
+			     struct ieee80211_vif *vif)
 {
 	return rtwdev->hci.type == RTW89_HCI_TYPE_USB &&
 	       vif && vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP;
 }
 
 static int rtw89_ops_set_key(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, enum set_key_cmd cmd,
@@ -984,7 +986,7 @@ static int rtw89_ops_set_key(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, enum set_key_cmd cmd,
 		/*
 		 * USB AP teardown frequently reaches key removal before the MAC
 		 * DLE fully drains. Skip the global queue flush in this path and
 		 * let station disconnect proceed instead of timing out here.
 		 */
-		if (!rtw89_ops_skip_usb_ap_key_disable_flush(rtwdev, vif)) {
+		if (!rtw89_is_usb_ap(rtwdev, vif)) {
 			rtw89_hci_flush_queues(rtwdev, BIT(rtwdev->hw->queues) - 1,
 				       false);
 			rtw89_mac_flush_txq(rtwdev, BIT(rtwdev->hw->queues) - 1, false);
@@ -1046,10 +1048,17 @@ static void rtw89_ops_flush(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 {
 	struct rtw89_dev *rtwdev = hw->priv;
 
 	mutex_lock(&rtwdev->mutex);
 	rtw89_hci_flush_queues(rtwdev, queues, drop);
-	rtw89_mac_flush_txq(rtwdev, queues, drop);
+	/*
+	 * mac80211 calls ops_flush on every station disconnect to drain the
+	 * station's TX queue.  On USB in AP mode the MAC DLE times out (50 ms
+	 * window too short for USB latency), leaving DLE state corrupted.
+	 * After many such disconnects the corruption accumulates until the AP
+	 * stops beaconing.  The HCI-level flush above is sufficient; skip the
+	 * MAC-level flush for USB AP vifs.
+	 */
+	if (!rtw89_is_usb_ap(rtwdev, vif))
+		rtw89_mac_flush_txq(rtwdev, queues, drop);
 	mutex_unlock(&rtwdev->mutex);
 }
